{"text": "When we say that water is clean, we do not just mean that it looks like a glass of water. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Water quality is about following a certain set of criteria, or benchmarks. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> These guidelines inform us exactly how much physical, chemical, or biological stuff can be in the water. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> These rules ensure the water is safe for anything we want to do with it, whether that is drinking it at home, watering crops on a farm, or running it through a huge industrial boiler. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> We cannot utilize the same one size fits all rule for everyone because we use water for so many diverse things. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For instance, the water that cools down a huge power plant generator does not need to be as clean as the water you drink from the kitchen tap. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This is why groups set different safety limits for the water dependent on how it will be utilized.", "alignment": {"characters": ["W", "h", "e", "n", " ", "w", "e", " ", "s", "a", "y", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "w", "a", "t", "e", "r", " ", "i", "s", " ", "c", "l", "e", "a", "n", ",", " ", "w", "e", " ", "d", "o", " ", "n", "o", "t", " ", "j", "u", "s", "t", " ", "m", "e", "a", "n", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "i", "t", " ", "l", "o", "o", "k", "s", " ", "l", "i", "k", "e", " ", "a", " ", "g", "l", "a", "s", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "w", "a", "t", "e", "r", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "W", "a", "t", "e", "r", " ", "q", "u", "a", "l", "i", "t", "y", " ", "i", "s", " ", "a", "b", "o", "u", "t", " ", "f", "o", "l", "l", "o", "w", "i", "n", "g", " ", "a", " ", "c", "e", "r", "t", "a", "i", "n", " ", "s", "e", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "c", "r", "i", "t", "e", "r", "i", "a", ",", " ", "o", "r", " ", "b", "e", "n", "c", "h", "m", "a", "r", "k", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0",